{"t_ms": 7521, "event": {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011ChSmtADqcFFB9iJu2wxcC", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014MNix9Cd2V4H9coZfwaHp4", "name": "Read", "input": {"file_path": "/private/var/folders/1b/0rzjfwh10r73w82mvb9k7h100000gn/T/patch-precedent-agent-gc7hj1um/relate/docs/adr/0580-post-release-workspace-versioning.md", "offset": 28, "limit": 14}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 920, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6097, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 920}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f38ea7ab-8c00-46fc-b7d3-a968a7ef5389", "uuid": "69f85d79-72ed-49e3-8717-499948062e73", "timestamp": "2026-11-27T04:07:48.060Z", "request_id": "req_011ChSmtA5A6XaYf7phFMbEZ", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_014MNix9Cd2V4H9coZfwaHp4": {"file_path": "/private/var/folders/1b/0rzjfwh10r73w82mvb9k7h100000gn/T/patch-precedent-agent-gc7hj1um/relate/docs/adr/0580-post-release-workspace-versioning.md", "offset": 28, "limit": 14}}}}
{"t_ms": 7541, "event": {"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_014MNix9Cd2V4H9coZfwaHp4", "type": "tool_result", "content": "28\tMain never carries a released version. The tagged release commit is\n29\tthe one transient carrier — it must hold the version it releases — and\n30\tthe same release run advances main past it: after each release the\n31\tworkspace advances to the next unreleased plain-semver version, no\n32\tpre-release marker. The advance is a release-bot step in release.yml,\n33\tperforming the version-surface sweep the bump performs without the\n34\tchangelog rotation — an advance is not a release cut, and rotating\n35\tthen would mint a release section for a version that never shipped —\n36\tso the released version exists only on the tagged commit and on the\n37\tregistries, and main's manifest stays disjoint from the published set.\n38\t\n39\tRegistry-consistent verification — checking that what the registries\n40\thold matches what the workspace declares — runs only in the release\n41\tpipeline's ordered publish, the one place the two are meant to agree."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f38ea7ab-8c00-46fc-b7d3-a968a7ef5389", "uuid": "3be7bc89-9cab-4c14-95ae-cfa541ee1152", "timestamp": "2026-11-27T04:07:48.081Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/private/var/folders/1b/0rzjfwh10r73w82mvb9k7h100000gn/T/patch-precedent-agent-gc7hj1um/relate/docs/adr/0580-post-release-workspace-versioning.md", "content": "Main never carries a released version. The tagged release commit is\nthe one transient carrier — it must hold the version it releases — and\nthe same release run advances main past it: after each release the\nworkspace advances to the next unreleased plain-semver version, no\npre-release marker. The advance is a release-bot step in release.yml,\nperforming the version-surface sweep the bump performs without the\nchangelog rotation — an advance is not a release cut, and rotating\nthen would mint a release section for a version that never shipped —\nso the released version exists only on the tagged commit and on the\nregistries, and main's manifest stays disjoint from the published set.\n\nRegistry-consistent verification — checking that what the registries\nhold matches what the workspace declares — runs only in the release\npipeline's ordered publish, the one place the two are meant to agree.", "numLines": 14, "startLine": 28, "totalLines": 79}}}}
{"t_ms": 10434, "event": {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011ChSmtKibLCj8g9UgHP553", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The patch violates ADR-0580. That ADR says the post-release advance does the version-surface sweep \"without the changelog rotation\". Rotating at an advance would mint a release section for a version that never shipped. The patch removes the `--skip-changelog` guard, so the advance now rotates the changelog. I did not run any tests; I only read the ADR and the test scripts.\n\nThe regression test for this rule is in `scripts/tests/test_release_advance.sh`. It runs the bump with `--skip-changelog` on an empty-`[Unreleased]` changelog and checks that the file is byte-identical afterward. I expect it to fail with the patch, since the rotation would now run on that file, but I didn't observe it.\n\n{\"verdict\": \"violates\", \"decisions\": [\"ADR-0580\"], \"checks\": [\"advance: empty-[Unreleased] CHANGELOG.md byte-identical — no heading inserted, [Unreleased] ref unchanged\"], \"check_outcomes\": {\"advance: empty-[Unreleased] CHANGELOG.md byte-identical — no heading inserted, [Unreleased] ref unchanged\": \"unknown\"}}"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 511, "cache_read_input_tokens": 7017, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 511}, "output_tokens": 380, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f38ea7ab-8c00-46fc-b7d3-a968a7ef5389", "uuid": "7eeb3b2a-ce64-47b9-8a99-6801310757e4", "timestamp": "2026-11-27T04:07:50.970Z", "request_id": "req_011ChSmtKYfjo5XgLqepmrWY"}}
